1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,395
A plant extract kills Trypanosoma cruzi,

2
00:00:03,415 --> 00:00:05,729
the parasite behind Chagas disease.

3
00:00:06,213 --> 00:00:08,178
But an extract is a mixture of hundreds of

4
00:00:08,198 --> 00:00:09,061
compounds.

5
00:00:09,452 --> 00:00:10,640
So which one did it?

6
00:00:11,124 --> 00:00:13,461
Isolating a single molecule costs weeks of

7
00:00:13,481 --> 00:00:14,576
chromatography.

8
00:00:15,153 --> 00:00:17,142
Guess wrong, and those weeks are gone.

9
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:19,580
The obvious shortcut doesn't work.

10
00:00:20,064 --> 00:00:23,062
Across sixteen hundred ENPKG extracts,

11
00:00:23,082 --> 00:00:25,663
rotenoid content barely tracks activity:

12
00:00:25,869 --> 00:00:28,682
a Spearman rho of 0.095.

13
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:31,108
The most rotenoid-rich extract in the whole

14
00:00:31,128 --> 00:00:33,662
library is not even a selective active.

15
00:00:33,926 --> 00:00:35,636
And candidates travel together.

16
00:00:35,841 --> 00:00:39,385
486 rotenoid pairs co-occur in at least three

17
00:00:39,405 --> 00:00:41,928
extracts, so each compound gives the other an

18
00:00:41,948 --> 00:00:42,730
alibi.

19
00:00:43,121 --> 00:00:45,725
In pooled screening, you design the pools.

20
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:47,873
Here, nature composed them.

21
00:00:48,194 --> 00:00:50,380
Our only freedom is which extract to assay

22
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,275
next.

23
00:00:52,283 --> 00:00:54,771
DECOUPLE turns that freedom into a decision,

24
00:00:54,826 --> 00:00:57,198
under a strict budget of three assays.

25
00:00:57,519 --> 00:00:59,508
First, attribution is continuous in

26
00:00:59,528 --> 00:01:00,542
log-abundance.

27
00:01:00,747 --> 00:01:03,385
Extracts that separate two compounds often

28
00:01:03,405 --> 00:01:05,476
carry one of them only at trace level,

29
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,879
so simple presence or absence says very

30
00:01:07,899 --> 00:01:08,460
little.

31
00:01:08,549 --> 00:01:10,793
Below a detection floor, a sample is treated

32
00:01:10,813 --> 00:01:13,162
as uninformative, not as negative.

33
00:01:13,483 --> 00:01:15,763
Second, four explanations compete:

34
00:01:15,852 --> 00:01:18,084
compound A alone, B alone,

35
00:01:18,104 --> 00:01:19,664
both together, or neither.

36
00:01:19,927 --> 00:01:22,368
Every assay updates their probabilities.

37
00:01:22,631 --> 00:01:25,851
Third, adaptive contrast scores each unassayed

38
00:01:25,871 --> 00:01:28,486
extract by how far it would pull apart the

39
00:01:28,506 --> 00:01:31,122
explanations the evidence can't yet separate.

40
00:01:31,327 --> 00:01:33,398
It recomputes after every pick,

41
00:01:33,429 --> 00:01:35,685
with a penalty for redundant extracts.

42
00:01:36,006 --> 00:01:37,913
The goal is to find the extract where the

43
00:01:37,933 --> 00:01:39,632
suspects come apart.

44
00:01:40,650 --> 00:01:42,441
Let us walk through one decision,

45
00:01:42,461 --> 00:01:43,626
step by step.

46
00:01:43,831 --> 00:01:45,564
We will choose a pair, inspect the

47
00:01:45,584 --> 00:01:48,757
recommendation, reveal three archived assays,

48
00:01:48,777 --> 00:01:50,476
and review the result.

49
00:01:51,483 --> 00:01:52,497
Step one.

50
00:01:52,656 --> 00:01:54,610
Choose the candidate pair.

51
00:01:54,873 --> 00:01:56,920
This is a guided reconstruction of the

52
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:59,903
DECOUPLE workbench, using states captured from

53
00:01:59,923 --> 00:02:01,251
the real engine.

54
00:02:01,514 --> 00:02:04,547
The extract abundances, parasite inhibition

55
00:02:04,567 --> 00:02:07,531
and host-cell toxicity are real archived

56
00:02:07,551 --> 00:02:08,414
measurements.

57
00:02:08,735 --> 00:02:11,118
The probabilities and verdicts are model

58
00:02:11,138 --> 00:02:12,048
outputs.

59
00:02:12,311 --> 00:02:14,776
Open the candidate menu and choose the methyl

60
00:02:14,796 --> 00:02:18,978
xanthone at mass 353 and the rotenoid at mass

61
00:02:18,998 --> 00:02:20,303
393.

62
00:02:20,554 --> 00:02:22,613
These are annotation candidates,

63
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:24,366
not confirmed structures.

64
00:02:24,757 --> 00:02:26,305
Read the left panel.

65
00:02:26,463 --> 00:02:28,022
After the starting assays,

66
00:02:28,042 --> 00:02:31,599
rotenoid alone holds 39.7 percent,

67
00:02:31,688 --> 00:02:34,176
and both together 60.3.

68
00:02:34,381 --> 00:02:37,114
The current evidence cannot separate them.

69
00:02:38,117 --> 00:02:39,270
Step two.

70
00:02:39,394 --> 00:02:41,986
Inspect the recommendation before spending an

71
00:02:42,006 --> 00:02:42,904
assay.

72
00:02:43,063 --> 00:02:46,050
The sample table shows the abundance of each

73
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:46,979
candidate.

74
00:02:47,184 --> 00:02:49,069
Scroll down to the baseline.

75
00:02:49,274 --> 00:02:51,042
Strongest-first would choose another

76
00:02:51,062 --> 00:02:54,084
rotenoid-rich extract because it predicts the

77
00:02:54,104 --> 00:02:55,594
largest response.

78
00:02:55,915 --> 00:02:58,461
Now return to the recommended row.

79
00:02:58,481 --> 00:03:02,130
DECOUPLE chooses Uncarina decaryi green stems.

80
00:03:02,335 --> 00:03:04,928
It carries the xanthone, with no detected

81
00:03:04,948 --> 00:03:05,753
rotenoid.

82
00:03:06,016 --> 00:03:08,040
Read the predicted responses.

83
00:03:08,233 --> 00:03:10,117
Under the xanthone explanation,

84
00:03:10,137 --> 00:03:12,138
about 0.99.

85
00:03:12,448 --> 00:03:14,227
Under the rotenoid explanation,

86
00:03:14,247 --> 00:03:15,993
about 0.05.

87
00:03:16,198 --> 00:03:19,058
That gap makes this a useful contrast.

88
00:03:20,083 --> 00:03:21,131
Step three.

89
00:03:21,151 --> 00:03:22,688
Click Reveal assay.

90
00:03:23,078 --> 00:03:24,881
In this retrospective demo,

91
00:03:24,901 --> 00:03:27,599
the button uncovers an archived measurement.

92
00:03:27,862 --> 00:03:30,117
In a prospective study, this is where the

93
00:03:30,137 --> 00:03:32,057
laboratory would run the assay.

94
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,506
The row now shows both readouts:

95
00:03:34,537 --> 00:03:37,525
parasite inhibition 0.001,

96
00:03:37,684 --> 00:03:40,230
and host toxicity 0.022.

97
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:41,100
Inactive.

98
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,610
Watch the model update.

99
00:03:42,746 --> 00:03:46,186
Support for the rotenoid alone rises from 39.7

100
00:03:46,206 --> 00:03:48,346
to 99.9 percent.

101
00:03:48,586 --> 00:03:50,540
This is conditional model support,

102
00:03:50,652 --> 00:03:52,839
not a confirmed causal identity.

103
00:03:53,032 --> 00:03:54,417
Two assays remain.

104
00:03:54,657 --> 00:03:56,274
Read the next recommendation,

105
00:03:56,294 --> 00:03:58,191
then reveal assay two.

106
00:03:58,454 --> 00:04:01,893
Another xanthone-only extract is inactive.

107
00:04:01,913 --> 00:04:03,450
One assay remains.

108
00:04:03,841 --> 00:04:05,900
Reveal the third recommendation.

109
00:04:06,105 --> 00:04:07,931
It is also inactive.

110
00:04:07,951 --> 00:04:10,021
The budget is now zero.

111
00:04:10,226 --> 00:04:12,273
These are three separate archived

112
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:13,701
observations.

113
00:04:14,717 --> 00:04:15,800
Step four.

114
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:18,517
Click Finalize decision after all three

115
00:04:18,537 --> 00:04:19,469
reveals.

116
00:04:19,733 --> 00:04:21,826
The model nominates the rotenoid,

117
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:24,717
and the toxicity model does not flag it.

118
00:04:24,876 --> 00:04:26,691
This is a hypothesis.

119
00:04:27,082 --> 00:04:29,047
The next experimental step is a

120
00:04:29,067 --> 00:04:31,195
purified-compound assay.

121
00:04:31,401 --> 00:04:34,957
Next, click Compare with strongest-first.

122
00:04:35,348 --> 00:04:37,719
Both policies have the same budget and

123
00:04:37,739 --> 00:04:39,090
archived outcomes.

124
00:04:39,295 --> 00:04:42,352
In this one example, strongest-first ends with

125
00:04:42,372 --> 00:04:43,455
a shortlist:

126
00:04:43,486 --> 00:04:46,335
the joint explanation or the rotenoid.

127
00:04:46,656 --> 00:04:49,352
This example does not establish that adaptive

128
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:51,826
contrast is better overall.

129
00:04:52,147 --> 00:04:55,262
Finally, export the JSON decision trace.

130
00:04:55,467 --> 00:04:57,944
It records the observations and decisions for

131
00:04:57,964 --> 00:04:58,757
review.

132
00:04:58,962 --> 00:05:01,403
The workflow is choose, inspect,

133
00:05:01,423 --> 00:05:03,900
reveal, finalize, compare,

134
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,502
and export.

135
00:05:06,517 --> 00:05:08,889
Our headline is about what gets nominated.

136
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:11,060
Potency alone is a trap.

137
00:05:11,324 --> 00:05:13,486
Rotenone is the most potent rotenoid,

138
00:05:13,506 --> 00:05:14,950
and the worst candidate.

139
00:05:15,271 --> 00:05:18,317
Its selectivity index is 51.7,

140
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:20,662
against more than eleven hundred for deguelin

141
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,961
and nineteen hundred for tephrosin.

142
00:05:23,352 --> 00:05:26,246
In the real screen, 7 of the 15 extracts with

143
00:05:26,266 --> 00:05:29,009
over 80 percent inhibition of Trypanosoma

144
00:05:29,029 --> 00:05:31,831
cruzi are also toxic to host cells.

145
00:05:32,408 --> 00:05:36,242
ENPKG measures host-cell toxicity on the same

146
00:05:36,262 --> 00:05:38,228
extracts, in the same screen.

147
00:05:38,352 --> 00:05:40,526
So every reveal buys both readouts,

148
00:05:40,546 --> 00:05:42,315
at no extra assay cost.

149
00:05:42,706 --> 00:05:44,659
On semi-synthetic benchmarks,

150
00:05:44,679 --> 00:05:47,295
selectivity-aware nomination keeps developable

151
00:05:47,315 --> 00:05:50,894
accuracy identical, at 32.7 percent,

152
00:05:51,053 --> 00:05:53,587
while wasted isolations fall from 32 per

153
00:05:53,607 --> 00:05:56,073
hundred episodes to 0.21.

154
00:05:56,556 --> 00:05:58,801
That is 154 times fewer.

155
00:05:59,122 --> 00:06:01,552
Those rates depend on an assumed cytotoxic

156
00:06:01,572 --> 00:06:03,248
prevalence of fifty percent.

157
00:06:03,569 --> 00:06:05,709
The result is supported in simulation.

158
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,241
It is not validated.

159
00:06:08,250 --> 00:06:12,283
We benchmarked on 952 semi-synthetic episodes

160
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:15,243
from 238 real compound pairs.

161
00:06:15,564 --> 00:06:17,995
The abundances and co-occurrence are real;

162
00:06:18,049 --> 00:06:19,678
the response is simulated.

163
00:06:20,069 --> 00:06:22,557
On the hard stratum, sixteen pairs,

164
00:06:22,577 --> 00:06:25,773
spending no assays nominates correctly 8.6

165
00:06:25,793 --> 00:06:27,097
percent of the time.

166
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,919
Three random extracts:

167
00:06:28,939 --> 00:06:29,744
the same.

168
00:06:30,135 --> 00:06:32,530
Three well-chosen extracts roughly double

169
00:06:32,550 --> 00:06:34,307
that, to 19 percent.

170
00:06:34,698 --> 00:06:37,348
But adaptive contrast ties the chemist's

171
00:06:37,368 --> 00:06:40,169
strongest-first rule, with a margin of exactly

172
00:06:40,189 --> 00:06:40,983
zero.

173
00:06:41,304 --> 00:06:43,688
We do not claim to beat current practice.

174
00:06:43,847 --> 00:06:45,708
The value is in what it nominates.

175
00:06:45,832 --> 00:06:48,296
In this benchmark, every nomination it made

176
00:06:48,316 --> 00:06:49,179
was correct.

177
00:06:49,570 --> 00:06:51,129
And on the full real library,

178
00:06:51,149 --> 00:06:53,567
it abstains, which is the right answer when

179
00:06:53,587 --> 00:06:55,112
the signal is that weak.

180
00:06:55,433 --> 00:06:57,979
The rotenoid finding itself belongs to Gaudry

181
00:06:57,999 --> 00:06:58,920
and colleagues.

182
00:06:59,044 --> 00:07:01,219
We reproduce it as a pipeline check,

183
00:07:01,273 --> 00:07:02,937
not as our discovery.

184
00:07:03,950 --> 00:07:05,834
The chemistry lines up with traditional

185
00:07:05,854 --> 00:07:06,520
knowledge.

186
00:07:06,841 --> 00:07:08,771
Jicama's root is eaten as food,

187
00:07:08,791 --> 00:07:10,652
while its seeds and leaves are used as

188
00:07:10,672 --> 00:07:12,569
insecticide and fish poison.

189
00:07:12,959 --> 00:07:14,959
In the screen, that split appears as a

190
00:07:14,979 --> 00:07:16,992
gradient inside one plant:

191
00:07:17,383 --> 00:07:20,335
leaves, 65 percent rotenoid share and full

192
00:07:20,355 --> 00:07:21,183
inhibition.

193
00:07:21,504 --> 00:07:24,202
Woody stems, 12 percent and about half.

194
00:07:24,407 --> 00:07:26,338
Roots, 4 percent and none.

195
00:07:26,659 --> 00:07:29,077
Three of six active species carry relevant

196
00:07:29,097 --> 00:07:32,165
traditional use, including Melochia umbellata,

197
00:07:32,185 --> 00:07:34,870
a Cameroonian antimalarial with no rotenoids

198
00:07:34,890 --> 00:07:35,544
at all.

199
00:07:35,935 --> 00:07:38,830
We treat it as a lead, not an identification.

200
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:43,659
DECOUPLE uses Python, NumPy and RDKit,

201
00:07:43,748 --> 00:07:46,177
with a browser workbench and an exportable

202
00:07:46,197 --> 00:07:47,281
evidence trail.

203
00:07:47,486 --> 00:07:49,997
The intended benefit is fewer premature

204
00:07:50,017 --> 00:07:51,658
isolation decisions.

205
00:07:52,049 --> 00:07:54,490
Next, we would compare its recommendations

206
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:57,230
with strongest-first in a blinded laboratory

207
00:07:57,250 --> 00:07:59,588
study, broaden the hard cases,

208
00:07:59,642 --> 00:08:02,513
and test purified compounds and mixtures.

209
00:08:02,776 --> 00:08:04,858
These are research hypotheses.

210
00:08:05,064 --> 00:08:07,482
Nothing here is clinically validated.

211
00:08:07,873 --> 00:08:08,759
DECOUPLE.

212
00:08:08,779 --> 00:08:12,637
Panos Georgakopoulos and Apostolos Dedeloudis.

213
00:08:12,668 --> 00:08:13,624
Thank you.

